{
  "base_commit": "e0df10d0bd5c7d8bcf3ae9bcab2ccf6a0ecfe7f4",
  "integration": "Original MusicController process lifecycle with passive pre-Term participation, exact original output/PostEvent/SetState return observation and a one-shot original startup trigger after exact owned queue success. Default off unless requested. Read-only track/context and scope-qualified resolved RTPC observations expose unknown failures without changing source dispatch. Streamed media is generated from the accepted full inventory and metadata and copied to the qualified original Android IO root before initialization; playback remains unqualified. The native source-skin lifecycle validates its original CharacterModel material cache through the retained source initializer before activation; this is a prerequisite, not visual acceptance. Bounded V1 waveform readback is separate from the retained schema-3 monitor ABI. It reads only after verified exact callback unregister/quiescence before Term, and persists private raw data synchronously after both returned Terms and verified monitor disarm; optional evidence failures do not replace original lifecycle failures. A separately selected, default-off LightningStake source-call observer snapshots bounded original pre-FireProjectile operands on the accepted integrated Nova routes; it does not change projectile behavior. A bounded read-only join samples the already-returned original music playing ID, event/segment/global-state results and passive capture callback/frame brackets during the exact selected music-output window; it neither changes playback nor claims output-event attribution or audibility. Ordinary requested audio may use the existing source Main Camera rig as a per-world non-rendering body/context owner; the explicit source-view diagnostic retains its own rig. Source callbacks and global camera/listener effects remain original. Teardown qualifies inactivity and managed-list removal separately from deferred destruction; native routing and audibility remain unobserved. Native network-sound catalog admission uses the original setter before world activation, validates complete source identity and nonzero name hashes, signals availability, and refuses missing or failed admission without changing the unavailable-audio decoder. Original empty event-name strings remain in the complete family and are passed unchanged to the original setter; null strings refuse before native mapping. Early source-count observations and bounded empty/null ordinals distinguish source values from native ID results. Initial audio-only camera admission waits for the original Start-assigned mode within a finite five-second window; activity/mode observations remain separate from values, and post-ready context loss still retires. Bounded scalar first/latest audio-camera admission observations survive retirement, with explicit unknown values, finite timing projections and unchanged source admission gates and music sampling cadence. The audio-only camera context queues creation during world preparation and begins once on the first exact-owned-body world-playing update; cleanup cancels a pending request before owner release. The source five-second deadline and readiness gates are unchanged. The integrated source equipment-highlight dependency is prepared from three exact typed owned catalog locations before body activation, holds its own handles through the session and stage changes, and restores only owned static assignments after verified body/model destruction and before catalog release. It preserves original equipment definitions, callbacks and prefab content.",
